      <rules>
        <rule name="Source Entry" id="r41-unit-xvi-0-justaerin-terminator-squad-source" hidden="true">
          <description>Justaerin Terminator | 5 | 4 | 4 | 4 | 2 | 3 | 2 | 9 | 2+/4+
Force Organisation:
CHOSEN OF THE WARMASTER A Sons of Horus Praetor, Ezekyle Abaddon or Horus Lupercal may select one Justaerin Terminator Squad as a retinue. If selected as a retinue, the squad does not occupy a separate Elites choice.
• Elites
• 0–1
Unit Composition:
• 5 Justaerin Terminators
Unit Type:
• Infantry
Wargear:
• Cataphractii Terminator Armour
• Foeblaster Boltgun
• Power weapon or Power fist
Special Rules:
• Legiones Astartes (Sons of Horus)
• Chosen of the Warmaster
OPTIONS
• The squad may include up to five additional Justaerin Terminators for +57 points per model.
• Any model equipped with a Power fist may replace it with:
• Chainfist ....................................... +5 points
• Any model may replace his Foeblaster Boltgun with:
• Combi-flamer .................................. +10 points
• Combi-volkite charger ........................ +10 points
• Combi-meltagun ............................... +15 points
• Combi-plasma gun ............................. +15 points
• Any model may replace both of his weapons with:
• Pair of Lightning Claws ....................... Free
• For every five models, up to two Justaerin may replace their Foeblaster Boltgun with:
• Heavy Flamer .................................. +10 points
• Reaper Autocannon ............................ +20 points
• Multi-Melta ................................... +25 points
• The squad may purchase:
• Banestrike Ammunition .................... +2 points per
eligible model
• Teleportation Transponders ................... +15 points
• One Justaerin may be upgraded to Falkus Kibre as described in his entry.
DEDICATED TRANSPORT
The squad may select a Land Raider, Dreadclaw Drop Pod or Spartan Assault Tank where Transport Capacity permits.</description>
        </rule>
      <rule id="r34-r41-unit-xvi-0-justaerin-terminator-squad-0" name="Legiones Astartes (Sons of Horus)" hidden="false"><description>All models with this special rule also have And They Shall Know No Fear as presented in ProHammer Classic. They are not Fearless unless another rule specifically grants Fearless. In addition, each model possesses one named version of Legiones Astartes corresponding to its Legion. A model may only ever possess one named version. Models with a named Legiones Astartes special rule gain any additional rules and abilities associated with that Legion. Unless specifically stated otherwise, Vehicles belonging to a Legiones Astartes army do not themselves possess the Legiones Astartes special rule.

And They Shall Know No Fear: Automatically passes Regroup tests at the start of the turn and may be used normally for the rest of the turn. If caught by a pursuit, the unit automatically regroups and is re-engaged in close combat, and does not suffer extra wounds from being caught in a pursuit. Immune to Fear.</description></rule></rules>
