      <rules>
        <rule name="Source Entry" id="live-r2-r41-unit-xvi-8-tybalt-marr-the-either-retinue-1-r41-unit-xvi-1-reaver-attack-squad-source" hidden="true">
          <description>Reaver | 4 | 4 | 4 | 4 | 1 | 4 | 1 | 9 | 3+
Reaver Chieftain | 4 | 4 | 4 | 4 | 1 | 4 | 2 | 9 | 3+
Force Organisation:
• Fast Attack
Unit Composition:
• 4 Reavers
• 1 Reaver Chieftain
Unit Type:
• Infantry
• The Reaver Chieftain is a Character
Wargear:
• Power Armour
• Bolt pistol
• Chainaxe
• Frag grenades
Special Rules:
• Legiones Astartes (Sons of Horus)
• Furious Charge
OPTIONS
• The squad may include up to five additional Reavers for +22 points per model.
• Up to two Reavers may replace their Bolt pistol with:
• Flamer .......................................... +5 points
• Meltagun ....................................... +10 points
• Plasma Gun ..................................... +15 points
• Plasma Pistol .................................. +15 points
• For every five models in the squad, one Reaver may:
• Replace his Chainaxe with a Power fist ......... +15 points
• Replace his Bolt pistol and Chainaxe with
a pair of Lightning Claws ....................... +15 points
• Every model other than the Reaver Chieftain may purchase:
• Terminator Honours ............................. +15 points
• The entire squad may take:
• Krak grenades ............................ +2 points per model
• Melta bombs .............................. +5 points per model
JUMP ASSAULT
The entire squad may purchase Jump Packs for +15 points per model.
If equipped with Jump Packs:
• the unit becomes Jump Infantry;
• it follows the normal ProHammer Jump Infantry rules;
• it may not select a Dedicated Transport.
REAVER CHIEFTAIN
The Reaver Chieftain may select up to 50 points of permitted weapons and wargear from the Space Marine Armoury and Sons of Horus Armoury.
DEDICATED TRANSPORT
A squad without Jump Packs may select a Rhino, Drop Pod, Dreadclaw Drop Pod or Land Raider where Transport Capacity permits.</description>
        </rule>
      <rule id="live-r2-r41-unit-xvi-8-tybalt-marr-the-either-retinue-1-r41-unit-xvi-1-reaver-attack-squad-r35-legiones" name="Legiones Astartes (Sons of Horus)" hidden="false"><description>All models with this special rule also have And They Shall Know No Fear as presented in ProHammer Classic. They are not Fearless unless another rule specifically grants Fearless. In addition, each model possesses one named version of Legiones Astartes corresponding to its Legion. A model may only ever possess one named version. Models with a named Legiones Astartes special rule gain any additional rules and abilities associated with that Legion. Unless specifically stated otherwise, Vehicles belonging to a Legiones Astartes army do not themselves possess the Legiones Astartes special rule.

And They Shall Know No Fear: Automatically passes Regroup tests at the start of the turn and may be used normally for the rest of the turn. If caught by a pursuit, the unit automatically regroups and is re-engaged in close combat, and does not suffer extra wounds from being caught in a pursuit. Immune to Fear.</description></rule></rules>
